Tokom izvještajnog perioda Udruženje zaštite na radu Crne Gore ostvarilo je značajan programski i organizacioni iskorak kroz dobijanje finansijske podrške za realizaciju projekta „Glas mladih za dostojanstven rad – od znanja do promjene“. Ovaj projekat predstavlja važan segment strateškog djelovanja Udruženja usmjerenog na unapređenje kulture bezbjednosti i zdravlja na radu, kao i na promociju dostojanstvenog rada, sa posebnim fokusom na mlade kao jednu od najosjetljivijih kategorija na tržištu rada.
Ugovor o dodjeli granta potpisan je 01. decembra 2025. godine, čime su formalno stvoreni uslovi za početak realizacije projekta. Planirano trajanje projekta je osam mjeseci, odnosno do 31. jula 2026. godine, što omogućava faznu, sadržajnu i sistematsku realizaciju planiranih aktivnosti, uz kontinuirano praćenje rezultata i ostvarivanje mjerljivih efekata.
Projekat „Glas mladih za dostojanstven rad – od znanja do promjene“ finansira Evropska unija, dok je njegovo kofinansiranje obezbijeđeno od strane Ministarstva regionalno-investicionog razvoja i saradnje sa nevladinim organizacijama, u okviru mreže YHWBT. Ovakav model finansiranja dodatno potvrđuje značaj projekta, njegovu usklađenost sa prioritetima evropskih i nacionalnih politika u oblasti rada, zapošljavanja mladih i jačanja uloge civilnog društva, kao i povjerenje relevantnih institucija u kapacitete Udruženja zaštite na radu Crne Gore za uspješnu realizaciju kompleksnih i društveno značajnih programskih aktivnosti.
Projekat je koncipiran kao odgovor na dugogodišnje izazove u oblasti informisanosti mladih o radnim pravima, zaštiti i zdravlju na radu i principima dostojanstvenog rada. Analize i iskustva Udruženja ukazuju na to da veliki broj mladih, naročito onih koji se prvi put susrijeću sa radnim angažmanom, ne posjeduje adekvatna znanja o zakonskim pravima i obavezama, niti o rizicima kojima mogu biti izloženi u radnom okruženju. Ovi problemi dodatno su izraženi kod mladih koji pripadaju ranjivim grupama, uključujući mlade bez zaposlenja (NEET populaciju), mlade žene, Rome i Romkinje i mlade sa invaliditetom, koji su češće izloženi neformalnim oblicima rada, nebezbjednim uslovima i ograničenom pristupu institucionalnoj zaštiti.
Osnovni cilj projekta jeste da se mladima omogući pristup relevantnim, razumljivim i praktično primjenjivim informacijama o radnim pravima, zaštiti i zdravlju na radu i dostojanstvenim uslovima rada, kao i da se osnaže za aktivno učešće u zaštiti sopstvenih prava. Projekat istovremeno ima edukativnu, savjetodavnu i zagovaračku dimenziju, čime se doprinosi ne samo individualnom osnaživanju mladih, već i širem unapređenju sistema zaštite na radu i radnih prava u Crnoj Gori.
Aktivnosti projekta planirane su tako da obuhvate različite nivoe djelovanja i da se međusobno nadopunjuju. U tom smislu, tokom trajanja projekta predviđena je realizacija sljedećih ključnih aktivnosti:
• sprovođenje edukativnih radionica i predavanja za mlade na temu dostojanstvenog rada, zaštite i zdravlja na radu i radnih prava, sa posebnim fokusom na učenike srednjih stručnih škola i mlade koji se pripremaju za ulazak na tržište rada;
• realizacija posebno prilagođenih edukativnih i zagovaračkih aktivnosti za mlade iz ranjivih grupa, uz primjenu inkluzivnih i participativnih metoda rada;
• uspostavljanje i promocija help-line linije i online „pravnog kutka“, kao dostupnog, povjerljivog i sigurnog kanala za informisanje i savjetovanje mladih o pitanjima radnih prava i bezbjednosti na radu;
• sprovođenje medijske i digitalne kampanje, usmjerene na podizanje svijesti javnosti o značaju dostojanstvenog i bezbjednog rada mladih;
• organizacija zagovaračkih aktivnosti i dijaloga sa relevantnim institucijama i socijalnim partnerima, sa ciljem unapređenja politika i praksi u oblastima rada, obrazovanja i omladinske politike;
• kontinuirano praćenje i evaluacija projektnih aktivnosti i rezultata, kroz prikupljanje i analizu kvantitativnih i kvalitativnih podataka;
• realizacija završnog događaja na kojem će biti predstavljeni rezultati projekta i razmotrene mogućnosti za nastavak i institucionalizaciju uspješnih modela djelovanja.
Dobijanje ovog granta ima višestruki značaj za Udruženje zaštite na radu Crne Gore. Pored obezbjeđivanja finansijskih sredstava za realizaciju konkretnih aktivnosti, projekat predstavlja potvrdu stručnog kredibiliteta i društvene relevantnosti Udruženja, kao i priliku za dodatno jačanje organizacionih kapaciteta, partnerskih odnosa i vidljivosti u javnosti. Posebno je značajno što projekat omogućava razvoj mehanizama podrške mladima koji imaju potencijal da ostanu funkcionalni i nakon završetka projektnih aktivnosti.
Udruženje će tokom cijelog perioda realizacije projekta redovno informisati svoje članove o toku aktivnosti, ostvarenim rezultatima i identifikovanim izazovima. Očekuje se da će projekat „Glas mladih za dostojanstven rad – od znanja do promjene“ dati značajan doprinos unapređenju kulture bezbjednosti i zaštite zdravlja na radu, jačanju svijesti mladih o njihovim pravima i odgovornostima, te stvaranju temelja za sigurniji, zdraviji i dostojanstveniji rad u budućnosti.

content_en:
During the reporting period the Occupational Safety Association of Montenegro made a significant step forward, both in programme and in organisational terms, by securing financial support for the project “Youth voices for decent work – from knowledge to change”. This project is an important part of the Association's strategic work to improve the culture of safety and health at work and to promote decent work, with particular focus on young people as one of the most vulnerable groups on the labour market.
The grant agreement was signed on 1 December 2025, formally creating the conditions for the project to begin. The project is planned to run for eight months, until 31 July 2026, allowing the planned activities to be carried out in phases, systematically and in depth, with continuous monitoring of results and measurable effects.
The project “Youth voices for decent work – from knowledge to change” is financed by the European Union, with co-financing provided by the Ministry of Regional Investment Development and Cooperation with Non-Governmental Organisations, within the YHWBT network. This funding model further confirms the importance of the project, its alignment with the priorities of European and national policy on labour, youth employment and strengthening the role of civil society, and the confidence the relevant institutions have in the Occupational Safety Association of Montenegro's capacity to carry out complex, socially significant programmes.
The project was conceived as a response to long-standing challenges in young people's knowledge of labour rights, occupational safety and health and the principles of decent work. The Association's analyses and experience show that a great many young people, particularly those taking up work for the first time, lack adequate knowledge of their legal rights and obligations and of the risks they may be exposed to in the working environment. These problems are even more pronounced among young people from vulnerable groups, including young people not in employment (the NEET population), young women, Roma and young people with disabilities, who are more often exposed to informal forms of work, unsafe conditions and limited access to institutional protection.
The project's basic aim is to give young people access to relevant, understandable and practically applicable information about labour rights, occupational safety and health and decent working conditions, and to give them the confidence to take an active part in defending their own rights. The project has educational, advisory and advocacy dimensions at once, contributing not only to the empowerment of individual young people but also to a broader improvement of the occupational safety and labour rights system in Montenegro.
The project's activities are planned to cover different levels of action and to complement one another. Over the course of the project the following key activities are envisaged:
• educational workshops and lectures for young people on decent work, occupational safety and health and labour rights, with particular focus on secondary vocational school pupils and young people preparing to enter the labour market;
• specially adapted educational and advocacy activities for young people from vulnerable groups, using inclusive and participatory methods;
• establishing and promoting a help-line and an online “legal corner” as an accessible, confidential and safe channel for informing and advising young people on labour rights and safety at work;
• a media and digital campaign to raise public awareness of the importance of decent, safe work for young people;
• advocacy activities and dialogue with the relevant institutions and social partners, aimed at improving policy and practice in labour, education and youth policy;
• continuous monitoring and evaluation of the project's activities and results, through the collection and analysis of quantitative and qualitative data;
• a closing event at which the project's results will be presented and the scope for continuing and institutionalising successful models considered.
Securing this grant matters to the Occupational Safety Association of Montenegro in several ways. Besides providing the funds for concrete activities, the project confirms the Association's professional credibility and social relevance, and offers an opportunity to further strengthen its organisational capacity, its partnerships and its public visibility. It is particularly significant that the project allows the development of support mechanisms for young people that have the potential to remain in place after the project's activities end.
Throughout the project the Association will keep its members regularly informed about the progress of activities, the results achieved and the challenges identified. The project “Youth voices for decent work – from knowledge to change” is expected to make a significant contribution to improving the culture of safety and health protection at work, strengthening young people's awareness of their rights and responsibilities, and laying the foundations for safer, healthier and more dignified work in the future.

Under the project “RIGHTS UP, RISE UP!”, supported through the programme “CSOs in Montenegro – from basic services to policy shaping – M'BASE”, implemented by the Centre for Civic Education (CCE), @Friedrich-Ebert-Stiftung, the Centre for Protection and Research of Birds of Montenegro and the Politikon Network. The project is financed by the EU Delegation to Montenegro and co-financed by the Ministry of Public Administration of Montenegro. The NGO Kuća organised the conference “Young people and decent work” on improving young people's labour rights and their safety and health at work, at which panellists and guests discussed the existing measures, the needs and the plans for further work in this field. The conference was held on 19 October 2023 at the Hotel Aurel.
The panellists were Đina Janković of the Occupational Safety Association of Montenegro and Ivana Mihajlović of the Union of Free Trade Unions of Montenegro.
The participation of representatives of NGOs, trade unions and the public and private sectors was key to considering the scope for improving young people's position on the labour market from several angles.
The subject raised a range of open questions about the inadequacy of public policy in this field and the need to improve it.
Starting from the undivided view that young people are a vulnerable group on the labour market, five main conclusions emerged:
- the need to insist on decent jobs for young people, and not merely on employment;
- the need to introduce occupational safety and health into Montenegro's education system;
- the need for continuous public advocacy and awareness-raising on this subject;
- the need for a multidisciplinary, cross-sectoral approach that leaves out none of the relevant parties;
- the need to provide educational modules for young people, in both formal and non-formal education;
- the need for continuous monitoring and evaluation of young people's position on the labour market.
These conclusions were supported by: the Women's Rights Centre, the Youth Initiative for Human Rights – Montenegro, the Association of Youth with Disabilities of Montenegro, the Network for Youth Activism of Montenegro, the Union of Free Trade Unions of Montenegro, the Trade Union of Administration and Justice of Montenegro, the NGO Juventas, the Bureau for Education Services of Montenegro, the Ministry of Labour and Social Welfare, ADP-Zid, the Roma NGO “Walk with us – Phiren Amenca”, the Chamber of Economy of Montenegro, the Ministry of Public Administration of Montenegro, the Sociological Association of Montenegro, the Centre for Civic Education (CCE) and Kuća.
It was agreed that a working group be formed to work together in the period ahead on developing these conclusions further.

content:
Privredna komora Crne Gore, u saradnji sa Sekretarijatom za podršku biznis zajednici Glavnog grada Podgorice, u ponedeljak 7.03.2022. godine, u prostorijama Privredne komore Crne Gore organizovala je seminar na temu „Medijski nastup“.
Predavač je bio renomirani novinar, sa višedecenijskim iskustvom – Saša Klikovac. Polaznici seminara su bili univerzitetski profesori, vodeći PR-i velikih državnih i privatnih kompanija, predstavnici ministarstava i lokalnih samouprava, medicinskih ustanova, civilnog sektora. Ispred Udruženja zaštite na radu Crne Gore, učešće su uzele Đina Janković i Ana Vuković.
Seminar je organizovan sa ciljem izgradnje kapaciteta, na način da, kroz prezentaciju i konkretne radioničke i individualne vježbe, nudi mogućnost prevazilaženja treme i izgradnje sigurnog, samopouzdanog javnog nastupa, pripremu govora, saopštenja za medije, itd. Kvalitetan javni nastup podrazumijeva poznavanje različitih oblika komunikacije i komunikacionih vještina. Radionica je bila interaktivna, a polaznici su tokom predavanja, mogli da postavljaju pitanja i diskutuju sa predavačem o izloženoj materiji, specifičnim situacijama i/ili problemima koje prepoznaju iz prakse ili iskustva.
Teme koje su na ovom seminaru obrađene su:
- kako pobijediti strah od medija;
- na koji način plasirati glavne informacije tokom medijskih gostovanja;
- priprema za TV, radijske i nastupe u štampanim medijima;
- verbalna; neverbalna i paraverbalna komunikacija (svjesno i podsvjesno);
- press konferencije: kada, zašto, kome, s kojim ciljem.;
- pravilan govor, dikcija, uklanjanje poštapalica;
- kako se obući za TV gostovanja.

content_en:
On Monday 7 March 2022, at its premises, the Chamber of Economy of Montenegro, together with the Secretariat for Support to the Business Community of the Capital City of Podgorica, held a seminar on “Media appearances”.
The trainer was the well-known journalist Saša Klikovac, who has decades of experience. Those attending included university professors, leading PR staff from large state and private companies, and representatives of ministries, local authorities, medical institutions and the civil sector. The Occupational Safety Association of Montenegro was represented by Đina Janković and Ana Vuković.
The seminar was organised to build capacity, offering — through presentation and concrete workshop and individual exercises — ways of overcoming nerves and building a confident, self-assured public presence, and of preparing speeches, press releases and so on. Good public speaking requires knowledge of different forms of communication and communication skills. The workshop was interactive, and participants could ask questions and discuss the material, particular situations and problems they recognise from practice or experience with the trainer.
The topics covered at the seminar were:
- how to overcome fear of the media;
- how to get your main messages across during media appearances;
- preparing for television, radio and print appearances;
- verbal, non-verbal and paraverbal communication (conscious and subconscious);
- press conferences: when, why, for whom, with what aim;
- correct speech, diction, eliminating filler words;
- how to dress for television appearances.

