Dana 09.02.2021. je održan sastanak u UZNR CG. Sastanku su prisustvovali Zdenko Janković, Đina Janković, Tijana Rakočević, Marko Milosavljević, Branislav Šebek, Nebojša Vujošević, Igor Bakić i Sanja Nešić. Od pozvanih članova, sastanku nije prisustvovala Slavica Grgurović.
Kao što je i u pozivu navedeno, sastanak je, u skladu s važećim epidemiološkim mjerama, održan u skraćenom sastavu, a ostali članovi udruženja/predstavnici ostalih ovlašćenih organizacija će o svom terminu održavanja satanka biti informisani u narednim danima.
Na početku sastanka, predsjednik UZNR CG Zdenko Janković je podsjetio prisutne na aktivnosti koje je udruženje realizovalo u posljednjem periodu, kao i na ulogu i značaj koji je udruženje steklo poslednjih godina.
Takođe je upoznao prisutne sa programskim ciljevima udruženja:
1. Uvođenje nulte tolerancije u oblasti ZZNR, što je moguće postići samo uz pomoć i podršku Ministarstva ekonomskog razvoja i Uprave za inspekcijske poslove;
2. Podizanje kulture rada i kulture zaštite i zdravlja na radu, za šta je neophodno podizanje nivoa svijesti poslodavaca i njihovo razumijevanje uzročne veze ekonomije/profita i zaštite na radu;
3. Uvođenja sistema kvalileta u privredna društva;
4. Uvođenje zaštite i zdravlja na radu u obrazovni sistem u Crnoj Gori;
5. Podizanje nivoa kvaliteta usluga ovlašćenig organizacija za poslove ZZNR;
6. Formiranje Nacionalnog savjeta za ZZNR, (u Evropi jedino Crna Gora i Albanija nemaju Nacionalni savjet za ZZNR).
Osnovna tema ovog sastanka je bilo pitanje unaprjeđenja usluga ovlašćenih organizacija, s akcetom na ono što utiče na kvalitet njihovog rada. Više puta je, tokom sastanka, skrenuta pažnja na ozbiljnost trenutne situacije, a čije posljedice će biti dugoročne ukoliko se ne reaguje na vrijeme. Napomenuto je da je razlog takve situacije možda u činjenici što nadležno ministarstvo, koje donosi rješenja i izdaje licence - nema instrumente kojima bi ista rješenja/licence oduzelo.
Kao jedan od problema istaknuta je i činjenica da se spisak ovlašćenih organizacija ne ažurira na vrijeme, što je nadležnost Ministarstva ekonomskog razvoja, a što onemogućava uvid u trenutno stanje – informacije o organizacijama koje su dobile nova ovlašćenja, odnosno o onima koje su ovlašćenja izgubile.
Navedeni su brojni primjeri iz svakodnevne prakse, pri čemu se posebno izdvaja problem nelojane konkurencije, nemogućnost uvida u sumnjive tendere, nepostojanje cjenovnog uravnotežanja i „dampingovanje“ cijena usluga, što se svakodnevno radi samo da bi se dobio određeni posao, pri čemu se npr.stručni nalaz o ispitivanju elektroinstalacija radi za 25 eura, a obuka zaposlenih, u vrlo rizičnoj metalnoj industiji, po cijeni od 5 eura.
Na ovaj način se unižava značaj zaštite na radu, nanosi šteta profesiji, ali u najvećoj mjeri poslodavcima i zaposlenima, koji za takve cijene dobijaju veoma loš kvalitet usluga. Postoje primjeri gdje se obuke zaposlenih uopšte i ne rade, već se izdaju blanko potvrde. Sve to u krajnjem dovodi do povećanja broja povreda, a poslodavci koji su izabrali duplo, a nekad i mnogo jeftiniju ponudu, trpe posljedice, do kojih neminovno dolazi. Prisutni su podsjetili da stručnost, kompetetntnost i odgovornost treba da bude na prvom mjestu, pa tek onda cijena.
Nebojša Vujošević smatra da Udruženje ZNR CG hitno mora zauzeti stav kako bi se ovakve i slične pojave spriječile. Napominje da je prošlo vrijeme ćutanja i da svako treba da radi u okviru svojih ovlašćenja. Ovo naglašava iz razloga što se često na terenu dešava da rješenja potpisuju oni koji za to nemaju ovlašćenja, a kao veliki problem navodi i dio inspektora koji ne rade svoj posao na adekvatan način, kao i diskutabilnost njihovih izvještaja. Zaštiti i zdravlju na radu se sve više pristupa menadžerski, a brojni su oni koji ne čitaju Zakon o zaštiti i zdravlju na radu niti znaju da ga tumače. On takođe napominje da će pokrenuti sva pravna sredstva, po cijenu gubitka rješenja, jer je ovakvo stanje postalo neodrživo, a to više nije samo pitanje zaštite na radu već pitanje časti, kulture i morala.
Kada su u pitanju koordinatori (K1 i K2) svi prisutni su saglasni da je to još uvijek velika nepoznanica i vrlo obimna tema, koja nosi brojne rizike. Skrenuta je pažnja da se mnogi prihvataju toga, dobijaju rješenja od nadležnog ministarstva o oslobađanju polaganja ispita i automatski stiču zvanje koordinatora, a nijesu svjesni obaveza i odgovornosti koje taj posao nosi. Takođe je postignuta saglasnost oko predloga za donošenje cjenovnika kad su u pitanju poslovi koordinatora, jer će se to u protivnom svesti na nivo stručnih lica za zaštiti i zdaravlje na radu, kao i oko organizovanja sastanka sa temom saradnje sa budućim koordinatorima, kako bi se zaštitila stručna lica.
Branislav Šebek je predložio da UZNR CG pokrene inicijativu za izmjene Pravilnika o postupku i rokovima za vršenje periodičnih pregleda i ispitivanja sredstava za rad, sredstava i opreme lične zaštite na radu i uslova radne sredine.
Usvojen je predlog da se preko Akreditacionog tijela dobije informacija o sertifikovanim kompanijama koje se bave standardima (ISO 45001) i da im se pošalje poziv za saradanju i dogovori sastanak.
Predloženo je da se u narednom periodu preduzmu konkretne aktivnosti povodom problema koji postoji već dugi niz godina, a odnosi se na rad sudskih vještaka, koji se više bave upravnim postupcima i pravnim poslovima, a manje vještačenjem.
Naglašen je i značaj predstavnika zaposlenih, koji se, nažalost, veoma rijetko srijeće u praksi kod poslodavca.
Na kraju sastanka je zaključeno:
1. Neophodno je utvrditi ko sve pruža usluge u ZZNR i da li to radi u okviru ovlašćenja koja ima;
2. Ispitati po kojim cijenama se pružaju te usluge;
3. Ustanoviti nivo kvaliteta pružanja usluga, ali će način dokazivanja toga predstavljati najveći problem;
4. U narednom periodu utvrditi termin održavanja sastanaka sa svim ovlašćenim organizacijama, po nivoima ovlašćenja;
5. Formirati i radnu grupu koja će se baviti gore navedenom problematikom.

content_en:
A meeting was held at UZNR CG on 9 February 2021. It was attended by Zdenko Janković, Đina Janković, Tijana Rakočević, Marko Milosavljević, Branislav Šebek, Nebojša Vujošević, Igor Bakić and Sanja Nešić. Of those invited, Slavica Grgurović did not attend.
As stated in the invitation, and in line with the epidemiological measures in force, the meeting was held with a reduced number of participants; the other members of the association and representatives of the other licensed organisations will be informed of the date of their own meeting in the coming days.
At the start of the meeting, UZNR CG's president Zdenko Janković reminded those present of the activities the association has carried out recently and of the role and standing it has gained in recent years.
He also set out the association's programme objectives:
1. Introducing zero tolerance in OSH, which is possible only with the help and support of the Ministry of Economic Development and the Administration of Inspection Affairs;
2. Raising the standard of working culture and of the culture of occupational safety and health, which requires raising employers' awareness and their understanding of the causal link between the economy/profit and safety at work;
3. Introducing quality systems into companies;
4. Introducing occupational safety and health into Montenegro's education system;
5. Raising the quality of the services provided by organisations licensed for OSH work;
6. Establishing a National Council for OSH (in Europe only Montenegro and Albania have no National Council for OSH).
The main subject of the meeting was improving the services of licensed organisations, with an emphasis on what affects the quality of their work. Attention was drawn several times during the meeting to the seriousness of the current situation, whose consequences will be long-lasting if it is not addressed in time. It was noted that one reason for this situation may be that the responsible ministry, which issues decisions and licences, has no instrument for revoking those decisions and licences.
One problem highlighted was that the list of licensed organisations is not updated in good time — a responsibility of the Ministry of Economic Development — which makes it impossible to see the current position, that is, which organisations have received new licences and which have lost them.
Numerous examples from everyday practice were given, among which the problem of unfair competition stands out, along with the impossibility of scrutinising suspicious tenders and the absence of price balance and the “dumping” of service prices, done daily merely to win a particular contract — with, for example, an expert report on testing electrical installations produced for 25 euros and training for employees in the highly risky metal industry priced at 5 euros.
This diminishes the importance of safety at work and damages the profession, but above all it damages employers and employees, who at such prices receive very poor-quality services. There are cases where employee training is not carried out at all and blank certificates are issued instead. All of that ultimately leads to more injuries, and the employers who chose the offer that was half the price — sometimes far less — suffer the inevitable consequences. Participants recalled that expertise, competence and responsibility should come first, and price only after that.
Nebojša Vujošević believes UZNR CG must urgently take a position in order to prevent such practices. He notes that the time for silence has passed and that everyone should work within the limits of their licence. He emphasises this because in the field decisions are often signed by people who have no authority to do so, and he also cites as a major problem those inspectors who do not do their job properly and whose reports are questionable. Occupational safety and health is increasingly approached in managerial terms, and there are many who neither read the Law on Occupational Safety and Health nor know how to interpret it. He also notes that he will use every legal means available, even at the cost of losing his own licence, because the situation has become untenable and is no longer merely a question of safety at work but one of honour, culture and morality.
As regards coordinators (K1 and K2), everyone present agreed that this is still a great unknown and a very broad subject carrying numerous risks. Attention was drawn to the fact that many take it on, obtain decisions from the responsible ministry exempting them from the examination and automatically acquire the title of coordinator, without being aware of the obligations and responsibilities the work carries. Agreement was also reached on the proposal to adopt a price list for coordinators' work, since otherwise it will sink to the level of safety professionals' work, and on organising a meeting on cooperation with future coordinators in order to protect safety professionals.
Branislav Šebek proposed that UZNR CG launch an initiative to amend the Rulebook on the procedure and deadlines for periodic examinations and testing of work equipment, personal protective equipment and working environment conditions.
A proposal was adopted to obtain from the accreditation body information about certified companies working with standards (ISO 45001) and to send them an invitation to cooperate and arrange a meeting.
It was proposed that concrete steps be taken in the period ahead regarding a problem that has existed for many years, concerning the work of court expert witnesses, who deal more with administrative procedures and legal matters than with expert examination.
The importance of employees' representatives was also emphasised, though unfortunately they are very rarely encountered in practice at employers.
The meeting concluded that:
1. It is essential to establish who is providing OSH services and whether they are doing so within the limits of their licence;
2. The prices at which those services are provided should be examined;
3. The level of service quality should be established, though proving it will be the greatest problem;
4. A date should be set in the period ahead for meetings with all licensed organisations, by level of licence;
5. A working group should be formed to deal with the issues set out above.

